WEBVTT

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.320
<i>Maybe this one?</i>

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.160
<i>It'll be for indoors, and black is easier 
to coordinate with other things.</i>

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.370
<i>That's huge.</i>

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.060
<i>Mima-san size.</i>

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.180
<i>L would be for Shun.</i>

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.090
<i>Let's go with this one.</i>

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:23.340
Excuse me, do you have this in a medium?

00:01:55.510 --> 00:02:00.010
<b>#14 
Nice Location</b>

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.820
Souma-kun, I'm over here!

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.360
That's too funny.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.640
You've made that mistake before, too.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.950
Please don't laugh.

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.980
That hardly sounds sincere
 when you're laughing too!

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.300
When you laugh, I can't help but laugh too.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.820
You always start laughing by yourself.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:19.820
It's totally obvious.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.460
Really?

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.890
Really really.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.620
No way. I thought I was 
doing a good job hiding it.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.990
This in medium, right?

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:28.140
Yeah.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.140
Pretty sure we have one.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:29.830
I'll go get it.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.450
You can keep looking around.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.730
Thank you.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.300
Want anything else for summer?

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:38.290
I recommend our patterned wear
 in the 'big silhouette' style.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.420
I wanted to go somewhere this summer,

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.030
so I'm trying to save some money.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.000
With a girlfriend?! Nice.

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:50.870
No. But I made some new friends recently, 
and I'd like to hang out with them.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.850
That sounds nice.

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:53.570
So where to?

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.120
I guess I haven't thought about it yet.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.830
That's so you!

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.370
But yeah, where should we go?

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.360
I guess an amusement park would be fun.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.760
Or we could go a bit further out
 and visit a hot spring.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:11.030
Where would you recommend?

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:12.820
As far as I'm concerned, 
there's only one option.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.380
Can't you tell?

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.360
My outfit is your hint.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.000
Being a pirate?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.830
Stop, you're making me blush.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.030
It wasn't supposed to be a compliment.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:23.670
Hello? The beach!

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:27.520
When you're young, in the prime of 
your life, the only choice is the beach!

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.220
You should go to the beach!

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.810
The beach, huh.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.310
The beach!

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.660
Let's see who can make it the farthest!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.030
Would probably sit under
 a beach umbrella

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:43.030
Would probably be 
satisfied with the sand

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.030
Would probably swim
 really far out

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.400
I feel like we'd be scattered all over.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.090
Are you planning on being shipwrecked?

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.850
We'll be putting out 
swimwear starting next week,

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:53.190
so come take a look, 
if you decide on the beach.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.050
Yes, I'll be back.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.750
So can I keep the clothes you bought?

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:00.740
No.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.420
You really are cute.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.030
You know, you have such a cute face,

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.930
it's a shame to hide that grin.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.570
So why are you always hiding it?

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:11.970
You self-conscious or something?

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.710
When I was in high school, 
I used to grin a lot,

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.360
m 0 0 l 170 0 170 33 0 33

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.360
Me in high school, grinning about 
something I remembered

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.940
<b>Grin</b>

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.940
and people always stared at me.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Stare</b>

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:19.400
<b>Sad</b>

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.910
I was probably being creepy.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.670
You really think so?

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.010
I was so embarrassed.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.270
<i>I think you've got it all wrong.</i>

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.830
So then, I decided to become 
this totally cool guy.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.380
And I haven't laughed since.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.490
Yeah, no, it's super obvious that you still do.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.210
<i>So it was that obvious, huh?</i>

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.670
<i>Then wouldn't that have the opposite effect?</i>

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.370
<i>Maybe I'm even creepier because of that.</i>

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.020
<i>That's a shock.</i>

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.160
<i>Oh yeah, a while ago, Asami-san said...</i>

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.410
And that's what you've been giggling about?

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.430
You're too funny.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:54.440
I think one of your strengths is being able 
to interpret even small things as positive.

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.920
<i>That's what she said.</i>

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.950
<i>But is this really one of my strengths?</i>

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.700
So you're an M, huh.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:07.960
I was sure you're an S.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.640
Where did that come from?

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:11.170
I'm not an M at all.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:12.660
But you are.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:17.180
I don't think I'm an S... or an M, really.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:18.810
Which one am I?

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:21.180
I think I'm just plain old normal.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:23.200
Well, I'm definitely an L.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.340
Fight it all you want, but you'll still lose.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:28.020
<i>Oh, he was talking about clothing sizes.</i>

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.380
<i>And somehow, I lost?</i>

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.830
What are you laughing about?

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.100
Because!

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.270
So this is it?

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:42.220
When you put it on, the 
sleeves fit perfectly.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.000
I personally like to have a little more room.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.410
I'm good friends with the guy 
who works at that store.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.610
He's really funny.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:49.980
This feels good. Lemme have it.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.150
No.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.670
Oh, right!

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:56.240
We should invite Hayate-kun and 
Mima-san to hang out this summer.

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:57.530
And do what?

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:58.720
Like, go to the beach!

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.250
The beach, huh.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.040
All right!

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.130
Let's see who can make it the farthest!

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:10.800
Would probably read, 
even at the beach

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.800
Would probably collect shells

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.800
Would probably get lost

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:10.800
Hey, where is everyone?

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.160
I feel like we'd be scattered all over.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.510
You think so too?

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:17.160
But how would we get to the beach?

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:17.950
By train?

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.530
I bet if we invite my older brother too,

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.120
he'd take us in his car.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:21.930
Powerful.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.110
Huh.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.430
I guess with an adult involved, 
you have more options.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:26.760
Let's go all over.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:27.690
Like overseas!

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:30.790
<i>I only just mentioned the beach,
 and he's already thinking bigger.</i>

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.010
What's that, you're planning 
a trip to the beach?

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:33.630
Yeah.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:34.950
That sounds fun.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.170
Oh, in that case!

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:38.530
I'll make you all bentos 
on the day you're going.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:39.370
Seriously?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.000
You're an angel.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.240
Asami-san...

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:43.840
You're so easy to read.

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:47.910
But if you're going to play hard, 
you also need to study hard.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:49.960
Ugh, fine.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.080
Good.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.720
Oh, Souma-kun.

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:57.430
You can go ahead and finish.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:58.470
Good job today.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:06:59.300
Okay.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.290
Maybe I should go home too.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:03.140
Souma...

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:03.770
Huh?

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.530
Let's go together.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:07.530
Sure.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.860
That was my first time 
watching a handball game.

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.690
It's really intense.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:14.860
It was really invigorating.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:16.330
Oh, yeah?

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.260
That reminds me. I didn't 
know you lived this way.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:22.210
It's in the opposite direction.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.910
Then this is a big detour 
for you. What's going on?

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:26.310
I wanted to take a walk anyway.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:27.660
Hmm.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.660
Huh, it's not changing.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:31.720
Yeah, huh?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.390
<b>Push to cross at night</b>

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.680
I knew that.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.420
Did you, though?

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:47.490
So, any time you want to notice...

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:49.700
Oh.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:49.690
Realization

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:52.220
Can I please have my cardigan back?

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:53.500
Don't forget it again.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:56.290
And you shouldn't wear it like it belongs on you.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.410
<b>Smoosh!</b>

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.410
<b>Smoosh!</b>

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:03.370
This has been bugging me for a while.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:07.330
You're a guy. You should just laugh out loud, already.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:08.340
Huh?

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:11.500
Why do you always try to 
hide it when you laugh?

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.670
But wouldn't it be creepy if I'm 
always grinning about something?

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:15.210
Huh?

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:16.630
Well...

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.970
<b>Grin Grin Grin Grin</b>

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:20.920
That'd be creepy.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:21.630
See?

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:24.850
I'm actually quite conscious 
of how people perceive me.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.400
<b>Hmmmmm</b>

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.400
<b>Hmmmmm</b>

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.060
<i>He didn't like that answer.</i>

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:32.970
The fact that you're so stupidly 
quick to laugh all the time...

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:34.610
Are you mocking me?

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.720
I like that about you.

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:39.830
So when you go and try to hide that,

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.290
of course I don't like it.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.500
So you liked that part of me?

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:50.270
Don't expect me to say that side of you is 
what gave me courage at my last match!

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:51.180
You said it.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.170
<i>His ears are bright red.</i>

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:58.100
I didn't know that was how you felt.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.230
I didn't say anything.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.960
Thanks, Shun.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.700
I'll try not to hide it so much from now on.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:05.130
Sure.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:06.620
Your ears are red.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:07.690
That's on purpose.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:08.620
On purpose?

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:09.770
What does that mean?

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:16.570
<b>Grump</b>

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:17.270
<i>I like that about you.</i>

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:30.010
<b>Smile    Smile</b>

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:25.770
<i>That's so cute.</i>

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:26.830
<i>He looks happy.</i>

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.510
<i>Maybe something good happened to him.</i>

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:29.990
<i>That's so cute!</i>

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:05.020
<b>Coming up next</b>

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:05.020
<b>Talking About Love</b>

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
